  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "opencode-go-keys-store",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "The explicit opencode-go provider kind adds session routing and a versioned User-Agent to keys checks and widens the SQLite profile store provider_kind CHECK set. Existing stores report migration-required until the Host calls migrateProviderProfileStore before opening; profiles and credential-store key references are preserved. Pi execution separately requires the declared pi_model.providerId and completions API.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#opencode-go-key-checks-and-profile-stores",
      "acceptance": "migrate",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/keys#MODEL_PROVIDER_VENDORS",
        "export:@byok-sdk/keys#ModelProviderProfileSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/keys/model-route#MODEL_PROVIDER_VENDORS",
        "store:keys-profile-store"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pi-opencode-go-provider-id",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "OpenCode Go profiles may set pi_model.providerId to opencode-go with an explicit openai-completions API to enable Pi reasoning_content replay and session headers on RPC and durable lanes. Other models must omit it; existing profiles need no change. Saving it changes the exact profile hash. The prepared lane refuses it, and keys-profile RPC launches refuse model-runtime composition errors instead of using a built-in fallback.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#pi-opencode-go-profiles",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/keys#PiModelConfigSchema"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "codex-session-store",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "The retention class agent-runtime-sessions is replaced by the expiring class codex-session-store: it is removed from PROTECTED_CLASS_IDS, ProtectedClassId and PROTECTED_CLASS_BOUNDS and added to EXPIRING_CLASS_IDS and ExpiringClassId, so replace the literal where the Host reads retention classes and treat the class as expiring. It covers the Codex rollouts that agentUserContext: excluded keeps under <Agent home>/.byok/codex. A rollout is deleted once its last write is older than the new DaemonConfig.storage.retention.ttlMs['codex-session-store'] (default 31 days, or the session-ledger TTL plus one day if longer; an explicit value must be at least that), unless a live session ledger still names its thread or its Agent home is running a task. Rollouts that used to stay until the Host removed the Agent home are now deleted by default; set the TTL higher to keep idle threads longer. Resuming a deleted thread fails closed through the existing non-retryable missing-thread path.",
      "migration": "docs/host-local-storage-layout.md#retention-bounds",
      "items": [
        "config:storage",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#ExpiringClassId",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#resolveStorageConfig",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#ProtectedClassId"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-memory-helper-protocol-4",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "Direct callers of openAgentMemoryFilesystemHelper must pass the required ancestorRoot from the canonical AgentHomeResolution.hostStorageRoot that owns canonicalHome. Upgrade the daemon and its SDK helper assets together: open requires protocol 4 and ancestorRoot, reports helper version 4, and rejects every other request/response protocol or helper version without a protocol-3 reader or default root. Source integrations using helperAgentMemoryIntentBackend must pass ancestorRoot second and move optional assetRoot to third. hostStorageRoot must already exist durably before the first open; creating that root is outside the barrier and tracked in #1652. Windows intent B remains false pending A7 recovery evidence.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#agent-memory-helper-protocol-4",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/agent-memory#openAgentMemoryFilesystemHelper"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "example-bot-collaboration-autonomy",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "Fix: the hosted Host (examples/hosted-bot-collaboration) now enforces Bot autonomy as the local Host does. An observing Bot records would-do entities instead of running create_routine, a cross-Bot delegate or room_call. A Host that vendors the example runs HostedCollaborationStore.migrate() once on every existing schema before the new code serves (it replaces entity_kind_check and moves any wouldDo rows left in a scope frame by an older L import into would_do entity rows), then calls setBotAutonomy(credential, botId, 'auto') for each Bot that must keep acting on its own.",
      "migration": "CHANGELOG.md#unreleased",
      "items": [
        "example:bot-collaboration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "adapter-session-limits",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "agy, dsh and Hermes accept fractional interruptTimeoutMs; session limits are defined once across six adapters.",
      "migration": "CHANGELOG.md#unreleased",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#AgyAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#ClaudeAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#CodexAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#DshAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#GrokAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#HermesAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#AgyAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#ClaudeAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#CodexAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#DshAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#GrokAdapter",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#HermesAdapter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "doctor-control-endpoint-refusal",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "DiagnosticsSnapshot.health gains an optional controlEndpointRefusal (code, path, recording time) on its valid branch. byok-agent doctor reports a typed control endpoint refusal instead of daemon offline. No Host change is required.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#doctor-names-a-refused-control-endpoint",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#DiagnosticsSnapshot"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "runtime-environment-lanes",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "RuntimeEnvironmentReport gains an optional lanes list (RuntimeEnvironmentLaneReport) naming the launch lanes that narrow the runtime environment and the names an SDK lane removes. No Host change is required; a Host that builds a report itself may omit lanes.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#runtime-environment-lanes-in-doctor",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#RuntimeEnvironmentReport",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#RuntimeEnvironmentReport"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "version-policy-source",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "The eight built-in adapter option types (Agy, Claude, Codex, Dsh, Grok, Hermes, OpenCode, Pi) drop the internal option that tagged whether versionPolicy came from the adapter option or daemon config. A Host that constructs an adapter directly deletes that tag from the options object (see the migration section for its name); versionPolicy and the version verdicts it produces are unchanged.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#version-policy-source",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#AgyAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#ClaudeAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#CodexAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#DshAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#GrokAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#HermesAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#OpenCodeAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#PiAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#AgyAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#ClaudeAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#CodexAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#DshAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#GrokAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#HermesAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#OpenCodeAdapterOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#PiAdapterOptions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "service-lifecycle-gate-root",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "CreateServiceLifecycleOptions gains an optional gateRoot: an isolated macOS root for the service-lifecycle gate, for tests and parallel consumers. Omitted, the gate root stays /tmp/byok-pm-<uid>. No Host change is required.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#isolated-service-lifecycle-gate-root",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#CreateServiceLifecycleOptions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "offer-selection-rules",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "@byok-sdk/protocol exports offerSelectionViolation, OfferSelectionRule and OfferSelectionViolation. TaskDeclineCode and the plaintext and sealed task.decline code enums gain agent_memory_selection_invalid, runtime_selection_mismatch and harness_selection_conflict, which the daemon now sends on its offer selection declines; an older Host reads them as unknown with reportedCode. A Host offer schema issue carries params.rule, and a payload that breaks several rules reports only the first. Breaking: @byok-sdk/cloud now refuses an offer whose custom harness the device did not advertise with agent_capability_missing instead of coordination_input_invalid (same message); a Host that branches on coordination_input_invalid for that refusal must branch on agent_capability_missing.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#offer-selection-rules",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#OfferSelectionRule",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#OfferSelectionViolation",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#offerSelectionViolation",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#TaskDeclineCode",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#TaskDeclinePayloadSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#TaskDeclineSealedPayload"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "per-runtime-environment",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "DaemonConfig.runtimes.<id> and RuntimeAdaptersRuntimes.<id> (PiRuntimeConfig for pi) gain an optional runtimeEnvironment: the environment policy of that SDK-built runtime, which replaces the top-level runtimeEnvironment for it and is not merged with the top-level pass. A runtime without it keeps the top-level policy, so existing configuration keeps its meaning. DaemonEffectiveRuntime gains an optional runtimeEnvironment, and byok-agent config check --json adds effective.runtimes[].runtimeEnvironment beside its unchanged top-level runtimeEnvironment. No Host change is required.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#per-runtime-environment-policy",
      "items": [
        "config:runtimes",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#DaemonEffectiveRuntime",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#PiRuntimeConfig",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#RuntimeAdaptersRuntimes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scope-key-package-v1-removed",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "Version 1 scope-key packages are removed (#1789). @byok-sdk/core no longer exports ScopeKeyPackageV1 or ScopeKeyPackageV2; ScopeKeyPackage is the one package type and sealScopeKeyPackage returns it, and openScopeKeyPackage refuses a version 1 package with key_package_invalid, so a recipient opens a package only when it names the recipient's KEM epoch. A device no longer re-wraps a version 1 package during a KEM rotation. @byok-sdk/protocol E2eeScopeKeyPackageSchema, the read shape, is now the version 2 shape for puts and reads, and E2eeScopeKeyPackageV2Schema is removed (use E2eeScopeKeyPackageSchema; ByokCloud and E2eeMemberStore put inputs name it). A Host read that meets a stored version 1 row fails the whole read with e2ee_member_state_unreadable; the put path already took version 2 only. Before upgrading, run the version 1 count check on every Host store; a Host with version 1 rows runs a KEM rotation on each affected member on the previous version first.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#scope-key-packages-are-version-2-only",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#ByokCloud",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#E2eeMemberStore",
        "export:@byok-sdk/core/sealed-payload#ScopeKeyPackage",
        "export:@byok-sdk/core/sealed-payload#ScopeKeyPackageV1",
        "export:@byok-sdk/core/sealed-payload#ScopeKeyPackageV2",
        "export:@byok-sdk/core/sealed-payload#sealScopeKeyPackage",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#E2eeScopeKeyPackageSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#E2eeScopeKeyPackageV2Schema"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "k4-transaction-rows",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "OutcomeTransaction and OccurrenceTransaction gain a required rows: ApplicationRows, the application rows of the same commit, as MessageTransaction has. A handler or hook that reads the transaction needs no change; code that builds one itself, such as a test double, adds rows.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#k4-transaction-rows-and-required-command-store-capabilities",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/server/execution-core#OccurrenceTransaction",
        "export:@byok-sdk/server/execution-core#OutcomeTransaction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "runtime-failure-category-removed",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "summary": "RuntimeExecutionFailure no longer has a category axis (#1758). The category field is removed from RuntimeExecutionFailure and RuntimeExecutionFailureInput, and the RuntimeFailureCategory type is no longer exported from @byok-sdk/client or @byok-sdk/client/adapters. Nothing read the field: retry stays the only retry authority and failure (TaskFailure) the only failure-class authority, and the wire projection (reason, retryable, failure) is unchanged. A Host or runtime adapter that passes category when it constructs a RuntimeExecutionFailure deletes that key; one that names RuntimeFailureCategory deletes the reference.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#runtime-failures-have-no-category",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#RuntimeExecutionFailure",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#RuntimeExecutionFailureInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client#RuntimeFailureCategory",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#RuntimeExecutionFailure",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#RuntimeExecutionFailureInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/client/adapters#RuntimeFailureCategory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "task-attempt-agent-ref-required",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "acceptance": "migrate",
      "summary": "Every task attempt has an Agent identity (#1780). TaskAttemptStore.open and TenantBoundTaskAttempts.open are removed; reserveAgentOffer is the only way to create an attempt. TaskAttempt.agentRef, the recordStatus agentRef, TaskArchiveWork.agentRef and server TaskSnapshot.agentRef are required. Postgres rows written without an Agent identity (builds up to v0.30.2) are retired by the operator: migration 0038 creates task_agentless_retired, the one-shot retireAgentlessTasks (cloud-dataplane, new) archives each terminal such task, removes its board item, moves it into that table and returns the count, and migration 0039 refuses while any remains, then makes the task Agent columns NOT NULL. Live ones are settled first on v0.41.0. A retired task id refuses a new offer with agent_task_already_exists; TENANT_ERASURE_TABLES gains task_agentless_retired; taskArchiveInput (cloud, new) is the shared archive input. Before that, a read that meets such a row throws the new CLOUD_ERROR_CODES member task_attempt_agent_ref_missing. The embedded SQLite schema moves to version 9 on open; the upgrade refuses a file holding such an attempt.",
      "migration": "docs/releases/host-upgrade-next-minor.md#every-task-attempt-has-an-agent-identity",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#CLOUD_ERROR_CODES",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#InMemoryTaskAttemptStore",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#TaskArchiveWork",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#TaskAttempt",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#TaskAttemptStore",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#TenantBoundTaskAttempts",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#taskArchiveInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud-dataplane#PostgresTaskAttemptStore",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud-dataplane#RetireAgentlessTasksOptions",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud-dataplane#RetireAgentlessTasksResult",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud-dataplane#TENANT_ERASURE_TABLES",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud-dataplane#retireAgentlessTasks",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud-dataplane/runtime#PostgresTaskAttemptStore",
        "export:@byok-sdk/server#TaskSnapshot",
        "store:cloud-dataplane-postgres",
        "store:server-sqlite"
      ]
    },
